From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:10:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the DS touch screen

sbar_nds.c draws the touch screen below the status bar with Quake's own
graphics. In a level it shows the map in the middle, following you,
with the level name, time and the keys, powerups and runes you carry,
the kills and secrets as percentages, centered, and at the bottom a cell
for each weapon, dark and without ammo until you have it, flashing when
picked up, the one in hand in a yellow frame. A tap on a cell selects
the weapon. When you are dead the map makes way for the kills, secrets
and time in the big numbers of the intermission, and how to try again,
instead of the scoreboard over the status bar, which shows no health below 0. The time stops when you die. While the menu is open the touch screen keeps showing the
game, with the options and while no game runs behind the menu it shows
the controls, in a dark inset in the middle of the console background.

The pictures of the weapons are drawn from their models when the game
starts: the ones you pick up, the axe and shotgun as you hold them, seen
from the side, textured and lit, with Quake's colormap. Which pixels a
triangle covers is worked out in integers.

The map is made of the walls of the world, a line for each face seen
from above (Sbar_BuildMap), a sloped one like a vault its bottom edge,
drawn once the renderer drew the face, the walls at your height brighter. It turns with you, you look up. It runs
from ITCM and is drawn every fourth frame while you move, the rest only
when it changes.
